AB  - With outdoor space as a place of multi-dimensional sensorial experiences, we decide whether it is pleasant to linger based on sensory judgments. With the virtual world of the internet, how to invite people to nature and how they interact with it have become an important issue in urban design. This paper explores multidimensional sensory experiences at diverse spatial scales and sensory preferences in order to enhance designers' knowledge of human perception in urban design, to identify the potential value of sensory experiences, and to create rich urban spaces.
