   This includes the physical features of neighborhoods including homes, schools, workplaces, neighborhood walkability/density, green spaces, transportation networks, and more that can influence overall community health.(1)
   Ecological Systems Theory
   Framework for understanding how a child's growth and development can be influenced by the child's micro and macro environments (home, school, community, and society), as well as by social interactions within those environments as proposed by Child Psychologist, Urie Bronfenbrenner, PhD.(2)
   Obesogens
   A class of environmental chemicals that disrupt metabolism (eg, through endocrine disruption) and as a result can promote weight gain.(3)
